anning to try to circumvent the free  market and think that the government  knows better than the market  or the entrepreneurs and the investors  ultimately bitcoin is a free market  technology anyone in the world with an  internet connection can plug into the  open system  and therefore the united states cannot  make the same mistake as china if  china's going to ban it if they're going  to outlaw it if they're going to put  pressure on their citizens and  corporations not to participate in the  ecosystem  thank you  we appreciate you  shooting yourselves in the foot while  the united states embraces this new  technology this technology is a freedom  technology it embodies everything about  the american ethos and values  it gives sovereignty and power back to  the individual it allows them to be able  to conduct transactions and transfer  value as simply as they can communicate  on the internet that's the beauty of  bitcoin and the united states just got  handed a second gift from china china  earlier this year banned miners and  kicked them out of the country thank you  we appreciate it because now the united  states has been able to gain significant  market share in the mining ecosystem we  appreciate that that makes the united  states more important in this industry  the future nation that ends up being  able to embrace artificial intelligence  bitcoin and decentralized technologies  will be the dominant nation  and that is what we have to continue to  beat the drum on here at home  now if all of a sudden china's going to  take that binding that mining ban  they're going to double and triple down  on it and they're going to say things  like now all cryptocurrency transactions  are illegal  thank you  we appreciate it that is exactly how we  position ourselves so that we can win  now on top of this we've got senator pat  toomey who came out and basically said  exactly this this is a united states  senator who was able to come out and say  china's authoritarian crackdown on  crypto including bitcoin is a big  opportunity for the united states it's  also a reminder for our huge structural  advantage over china  and so here you have a u.s senator again  talking about the authoritarian  crackdown on crypto in china  and saying that bitcoin is a big  opportunity for the united states it's a  reminder that we have a structural  advantage over china open networks beat  closed networks freedom trumps  authoritarianism that is what we know  democracy is better than communism and  socialism if you don't believe in those  things then you have a lot of questions  to ask because you may not be a student  of history and you may not actually  believe in the same things that america  was built on that free market  competition on a global scale if there's  a game put us in the game and let us  compete  that ultimately is going to decide who  the winner is let's go compete because  i'll always bet on american  entrepreneurs innovators and investors  to win on the global stage and even  better than that is that the pull of  america the promise of the american  dream the ability for people to come to  this country regardless of where they  were born what wealth they have what  education they have who their parents or  friends are what language they speak  what their sex is what their religion is  what their other beliefs are  they're allowed to come to this country  and when they come here they have the  ability to pursue a life of health  wealth happiness and financial security  that is the american dream is you can  come from anywhere in the world you can  come here and you can build that life  for yourself it's because we believe  that the individual is going to put us  in a position to be successful and  ultimately what we are watching is the  united states  has to make a decision china just made  theirs there's a line in the sand now  china says this freedom technology we do  not want inside of our country we do not  believe  that it aligns with our ethos  america if we value freedom should  embrace bitcoin we should be the leader  on a global stage we should say to  ourselves this decentralized digital  technology will allow us to continue to  be economically prosperous and it will  put us ahead of everyone else in the  world that's the beauty of bitcoin but  bitcoin doesn't care bitcoin doesn't  care if china embraces it doesn't care  if the united states embraces it doesn't  care if any other country embraces or  pushes it away it is nation agnostic  it simply continues to produce block  after block after block of transactions  and that's the beauty of bitcoin is that  regardless of whether you like it you  hate it  you want it to succeed or fail  it just keeps producing block after  block after block  we have circle ceo jeremy elaire he had  a whole tweet thread  this morning talking about these very  issues he said first a message to us and  western policy makers on how to think  about china's approach to crypto and  blockchain china opposes the western  system of values built on openness  transparency privacy free market  competition and so forth he then went on  to say  the next slide here that we have uh he  then went on to say that the internet  itself has an expression of these values  and it is one of the reasons that china  has always fought to control the  internet these values are also deeply at  the core of crypto and blockchains  enshrining them into new economic and  governance infrastructure and then the  thread went on and continuously said  crypto in blockchain is an absolute  threat to systems that are built around  total control centralization of power  elimination of privacy etc which side of  this do we want to be on  and then he said in the west a  rules-based order based on open free  market and democratic principles has  provided a very strong foundation for  economic and governance systems and have  the best hope of being extended by  embracing open public blockchains and